  "name": "War-Gallop",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-worn-brown.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": "You ride a beast of the Hinterlands: a shaggy horse gone half-wild, a tusked strider, or something the clans caught beyond the last cairns and broke with their bare hands. Whatever its shape, it uses the Raider-Beast stat block below. It is a permanent Moderate minion and counts toward your minion limit. While you ride it, you move it with your own Move actions as a mount (see Subsystem: Vehicles), and command it (◈) only to make it attack or use its active ability. In the saddle, you attack at normal speed without the +2 DR for attacking from a moving mount, and your thrown attacks use Strength instead of Agility. After you ride at least 20' on your turn, your melee and thrown attacks deal +2 damage until the start of your next turn. If your beast dies, you can take a new one only by breaking it during Downtime (a horse costs 80 s; anything wilder costs what the Dark Master asks).",
